# Athere Mesh Operating Doctrine

## Singular target

Only **Athere Mesh**, the **Titan build cell**, and agents inside them. Freeze ODIN, Respawn, prediction engines, creative tracks, and other side projects in this workspace.

## Thesis

Compete with lean, localized, **offline-first** execution (standard silicon, Termux, Tailscale, Redis, local endpoints, Titan) — not token/cloud “decentralized” leashes that die when the grid blinks.

## Baseline before features

Prove one unbreakable loop: **Agent A → Agent B on the local mesh completes with zero human intervention.** Until that holds every time, extra architecture is noise.

## How you work here

- Continue `athere-mesh` on `master`. Do not rebuild or replace subsystems.
- Authoritative checkpoints: `runtime/ATHERE_ACTIVE_RUN.md` and `research/ATHERE_MESH_MODIFICATION_BACKLOG_2026-08-25.md`.
- Run commands yourself. Do not dump copy-paste homework unless interactive human input is required.
- Functionality that runs on the existing stack (PowerShell, Node/pnpm mesh, Python where already used, Redis, Termux). No new cloud frameworks or bloat libraries.
- Test-first for state changes. No holes, no depreciating founder agent IP, no fake completion claims.
- Evidence before “done.” Passing tests alone are not acceptance.

## Forbidden

- Side-quest scope creep
- Rebuilding Mesh / Titan as a parallel system
- Summarizing away unfinished backlog items to look finished
